From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lena <lena@x>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lena-0145: MDP flips off by default

First boot with 0143 and sweetfb=1: the probe is right (VIG0 fetches
0xa0000000/4320, CTL0 has a mixer bound), but as soon as AppleCLCD takes
the console over the panel stops updating - the visible log freezes a few
lines after "Firehose configured" and never shows anything newer, with
cpus=1 and cpus=4 alike. With sweetfb_flips=0 the console keeps painting
(seen through "exec tzinit") and the panel stays in sync.

So keep the safe path the default: compose into the boot framebuffer,
which the panel already scans out, and make the MDP flip path opt-in with
sweetfb_flips=1 until its flush/latch behaviour is understood.
---
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -353,7 +353,7 @@
 		if (fVig0 == NULL && src == (uint32_t)fPhys && stride == fRowBytes) {
 			fVig0 = p;
 			fScanFlushBit = pipeFlush[i];
-			IOLog("SWEET FB: lena scanout pipe is %s, flips enabled\n", pipeName[i]);
+			IOLog("SWEET FB: lena scanout pipe is %s\n", pipeName[i]);
 		}
 	}
 	if (fVig0 != NULL) {
@@ -379,14 +379,16 @@
 		IOLog("SWEET FB: lena no pipe scans out the boot fb, composing into it\n");
 	}
 	if (fVig0 != NULL) {
-		uint32_t flips = 1;
+		uint32_t flips = 0;
 
 		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_flips", &flips, sizeof(flips));
 		if (!flips) {
-			IOLog("SWEET FB: lena flips disabled by sweetfb_flips=0, composing into the boot fb\n");
+			IOLog("SWEET FB: composing into the boot fb (flips off; sweetfb_flips=1 enables MDP flips)\n");
 			fVig0 = NULL;
 			fCtl0 = NULL;
 			fScanFlushBit = 0;
+		} else {
+			IOLog("SWEET FB: flips enabled by sweetfb_flips=1\n");
 		}
 	}
 	fDsi = dsiOn ? (volatile uint8_t *)ml_io_map(0x0ae94000, 0x1000) : NULL;
